IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`

-- Old Age Security Act, Part IV, "Benefits" (s 36) and the return and recovery of a benefit payment (s 37): a benefit cannot be assigned or
-- seized; what the Minister may deduct for a province, a municipality or the Department of Veterans Affairs; what a person must return when
-- paid too much; the debt that arises; and how the Minister collects it, remits it, or certifies it to the Federal Court.
-- Hohfeld: the person's immunity (36(1), (1.1)) is the creditors' disability; the Minister's power to deduct (36(2), (3), 37(2.1)) is the person's
-- liability; the Minister's claim to repayment (37(1)) is the person's duty; the Minister's power to remit (37(4)) is the person's liability.
-- Regulations s 27 (undue hardship) and s 28.1 (the conditions of a deduction under 36(2)) are piece oa3's, and arrive as inputs.

§ `Benefit not assignable`

-- s 36(1): "any transaction purporting to assign, charge, attach, anticipate or give as security a benefit is void".
-- src:958 | 36 (1) A benefit shall not be assigned, charged, attached, anticipated or given as security, and any transaction purporting to assign, charge, attach, anticipate or give as security a benefit is void.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 36(1) (src:958)
GIVEN `the transaction purports to assign, charge, attach, anticipate or give as security a benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36(1): the transaction is void` `the transaction purports to assign, charge, attach, anticipate or give as security a benefit` MEANS
    `the transaction purports to assign, charge, attach, anticipate or give as security a benefit`

-- s 36(1.1): "A benefit is exempt from seizure and execution, either at law or in equity": no seizure or execution may reach it.
-- src:960 | (1.1) A benefit is exempt from seizure and execution, either at law or in equity.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 36(1.1) (src:960)
GIVEN `seizure or execution is sought against a benefit, at law or in equity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36(1.1): the benefit is liable to the seizure or execution` `seizure or execution is sought against a benefit, at law or in equity` MEANS
    FALSE

-- s 36(2): "Despite subsections (1) and (1.1)": the Minister may deduct from the benefit and pay to a provincial or municipal authority an amount
-- not more than the advance, assistance or welfare payment, in accordance with the terms and conditions prescribed (Regulations s 28.1).
-- src:962 | (2) Despite subsections (1) and (1.1), if a provincial authority or a municipal authority in a province pays a person any advance or assistance or welfare payment for a month or a portion of a month that would not be paid if a benefit under this Act had been paid for that period and subsequently a benefit becomes payable or payment of a benefit may be made under this Act to that person for that period, the Minister may, in accordance with any terms and conditions that may be prescribed, deduct from the benefit and pay to the provincial authority or municipal authority, as the case may be, an amount not more than the amount of the advance or assistance or welfare payment paid.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 36(2) (src:962)
GIVEN `a provincial authority or a municipal authority in a province pays a person an advance or assistance or welfare payment for a month or a portion of a month that would not be paid if a benefit under this Act had been paid for that period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsequently a benefit becomes payable or payment of a benefit may be made under this Act to that person for that period` IS A BOOLEAN
      -- out of range: section 28.1 (piece oa3): Regulations
      `the terms and conditions that may be prescribed are met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the advance or assistance or welfare payment paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 36(2): the most the Minister may deduct from the benefit and pay to the provincial authority or municipal authority` `a provincial authority or a municipal authority in a province pays a person an advance or assistance or welfare payment for a month or a portion of a month that would not be paid if a benefit under this Act had been paid for that period` `subsequently a benefit becomes payable or payment of a benefit may be made under this Act to that person for that period` `the terms and conditions that may be prescribed are met` `the amount of the advance or assistance or welfare payment paid` MEANS
    IF     `a provincial authority or a municipal authority in a province pays a person an advance or assistance or welfare payment for a month or a portion of a month that would not be paid if a benefit under this Act had been paid for that period`
       AND `subsequently a benefit becomes payable or payment of a benefit may be made under this Act to that person for that period`
       AND `the terms and conditions that may be prescribed are met`
    THEN JUST `the amount of the advance or assistance or welfare payment paid`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 36(3): the Department of Veterans Affairs may be reimbursed up to the amount of the benefit it paid, if the person consented in writing on or before
-- receiving it. "the amount of the benefit" is taken as the amount received from that Department (fork OA1-F12 of NOTES.md).
-- src:964 | (3) Notwithstanding subsections (1) and (1.1), where any benefit is received for a month or any portion of a month after this subsection comes into force under any Act of Parliament that is administered by the Minister of Veterans Affairs, that would not have been received if a benefit under this Act had been paid for that period and subsequently a benefit becomes payable or payment of a benefit may be made under this Act to that person for that period, the Minister may deduct from the benefit and pay to the Department of Veterans Affairs an amount not exceeding the amount of the benefit if that person had, on or before receiving the benefit from the Department of Veterans Affairs, consented in writing to the deduction and payment by the Minister.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 36(3) (src:964)
GIVEN `a benefit is received for a month or a portion of a month, under an Act of Parliament that is administered by the Minister of Veterans Affairs, that would not have been received if a benefit under this Act had been paid for that period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsequently a benefit becomes payable or payment of a benefit may be made under this Act to that person for that period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had, on or before receiving the benefit from the Department of Veterans Affairs, consented in writing to the deduction and payment by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the benefit received from the Department of Veterans Affairs` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 36(3): the most the Minister may deduct from the benefit and pay to the Department of Veterans Affairs` `a benefit is received for a month or a portion of a month, under an Act of Parliament that is administered by the Minister of Veterans Affairs, that would not have been received if a benefit under this Act had been paid for that period` `subsequently a benefit becomes payable or payment of a benefit may be made under this Act to that person for that period` `the person had, on or before receiving the benefit from the Department of Veterans Affairs, consented in writing to the deduction and payment by the Minister` `the amount of the benefit received from the Department of Veterans Affairs` MEANS
    IF     `a benefit is received for a month or a portion of a month, under an Act of Parliament that is administered by the Minister of Veterans Affairs, that would not have been received if a benefit under this Act had been paid for that period`
       AND `subsequently a benefit becomes payable or payment of a benefit may be made under this Act to that person for that period`
       AND `the person had, on or before receiving the benefit from the Department of Veterans Affairs, consented in writing to the deduction and payment by the Minister`
    THEN JUST `the amount of the benefit received from the Department of Veterans Affairs`
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Return of benefit where recipient not entitled`

-- s 37(1): the payment, or the excess, is to be returned "forthwith" (the Act sets no number of days). Where the person was entitled to nothing, the
-- whole payment is the excess.
-- src:966 | 37 (1) A person who has received or obtained by cheque or otherwise a benefit payment to which the person is not entitled, or a benefit payment in excess of the amount of the benefit payment to which the person is entitled, shall forthwith return the cheque or the amount of the benefit payment, or the excess amount, as the case may be.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 37(1) (src:966)
GIVEN `the amount of the benefit payment that the person has received or obtained` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the benefit payment to which the person is entitled` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 37(1): the amount the person shall forthwith return` `the amount of the benefit payment that the person has received or obtained` `the amount of the benefit payment to which the person is entitled` MEANS
    max 0 (`the amount of the benefit payment that the person has received or obtained` MINUS `the amount of the benefit payment to which the person is entitled`)

-- (2): the amount "constitutes a debt due to Her Majesty and is recoverable at any time".
-- src:968 | (2) If a person has received or obtained a benefit payment to which the person is not entitled, or a benefit payment in excess of the amount of the benefit payment to which the person is entitled, the amount of the benefit payment or the excess amount, as the case may be, constitutes a debt due to Her Majesty and is recoverable at any time in the Federal Court or any other court of competent jurisdiction or in any other manner provided by this Act.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 37(2) (src:968)
GIVEN `the amount of the benefit payment that the person has received or obtained` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the benefit payment to which the person is entitled` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 37(2): the debt due to Her Majesty for a benefit payment` `the amount of the benefit payment that the person has received or obtained` `the amount of the benefit payment to which the person is entitled` MEANS
    `s 37(1): the amount the person shall forthwith return` `the amount of the benefit payment that the person has received or obtained` `the amount of the benefit payment to which the person is entitled`

-- src:968 | (2) If a person has received or obtained a benefit payment to which the person is not entitled, or a benefit payment in excess of the amount of the benefit payment to which the person is entitled, the amount of the benefit payment or the excess amount, as the case may be, constitutes a debt due to Her Majesty and is recoverable at any time in the Federal Court or any other court of competent jurisdiction or in any other manner provided by this Act.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 37(2) (src:968)
GIVEN `the day on which recovery is sought` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 37(2): the debt is recoverable on the day` `the day on which recovery is sought` MEANS
    TRUE

-- (2.01) and (2.02): interest payable under the Act, and a penalty imposed under section 44.1, are likewise debts due to Her Majesty.
-- src:970 | (2.01) Interest payable under this Act constitutes a debt due to Her Majesty and is recoverable at any time in the Federal Court or any other court of competent jurisdiction or in any other manner provided by this Act.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 37(2.01) (src:970)
GIVEN `the amount of interest payable under this Act` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: section 48 (piece oa3): Regulations, "interest"
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 37(2.01): the debt due to Her Majesty for interest` `the amount of interest payable under this Act` MEANS
    `the amount of interest payable under this Act`

-- src:972 | (2.02) The amount of a penalty imposed on a person under section 44.1 constitutes a debt due to Her Majesty and is recoverable at any time in the Federal Court or any other court of competent jurisdiction or in any other manner provided by this Act.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 37(2.02) (src:972)
GIVEN `the amount of a penalty imposed on the person under section 44.1` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 37(2.02): the debt due to Her Majesty for a penalty` `the amount of a penalty imposed on the person under section 44.1` MEANS
    `the amount of a penalty imposed on the person under section 44.1`

-- (2.1): the debt may be deducted and retained out of any amount payable to the person or the person's estate or succession under this Act or any other
-- Act or program the Minister administers, in the prescribed manner (Regulations s 27: in any amount that does not cause undue hardship). Not more can be
-- deducted than the debt or than the amount payable.
-- src:974 | (2.1) If any amount is or becomes payable to the person or to the person’s estate or succession under this Act or any other Act or program administered by the Minister, the amount of the debt may be deducted and retained out of the amount payable in the prescribed manner.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 37(2.1) (src:974)
GIVEN `the amount of the debt` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount payable to the person or to the person's estate or succession under this Act or any other Act or program administered by the Minister` IS A NUMBER
      -- out of range: section 27 (piece oa3): Regulations
      `the deduction is made in the prescribed manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 37(2.1): the most that may be deducted and retained out of the amount payable` `the amount of the debt` `the amount payable to the person or to the person's estate or succession under this Act or any other Act or program administered by the Minister` `the deduction is made in the prescribed manner` MEANS
    IF `the deduction is made in the prescribed manner`
    THEN min `the amount of the debt` `the amount payable to the person or to the person's estate or succession under this Act or any other Act or program administered by the Minister`
    ELSE 0

-- (2.2): the Minister may certify all or part of the debt that has not been recovered, (a) without delay where, in the Minister's opinion, the person is
-- attempting to avoid payment, and (b) in any other case on the expiration of 30 days after the default: the day after the thirtieth day (fork OA1-F13 of NOTES.md).
-- src:976 | (2.2) All or part of the debt that has not been recovered may be certified by the Minister
-- src:977 | (a) without delay, if in the Minister’s opinion the person liable to pay the amount is attempting to avoid payment; and
-- src:978 | (b) in any other case, on the expiration of 30 days after the default.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 37(2.2) (src:976-978)
GIVEN `part of the debt has not been recovered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the Minister's opinion the person liable to pay the amount is attempting to avoid payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the default` IS A DATE
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 37(2.2): the Minister may certify the debt that has not been recovered on the day` `part of the debt has not been recovered` `in the Minister's opinion the person liable to pay the amount is attempting to avoid payment` `the day of the default` `the day` MEANS
        `part of the debt has not been recovered`
    AND (    `in the Minister's opinion the person liable to pay the amount is attempting to avoid payment`
         OR  `the day` GREATER THAN (`the day that is` (`a limit in days` 30) `after` `the day of the default`))

-- (2.3): registered in the Federal Court, the certificate has the force and effect of a judgment for a debt of the amount it specifies.
-- src:980 | (2.3) On production to the Federal Court, the certificate shall be registered in the Court. When it is registered, it has the same force and effect, and all proceedings may be taken, as if the certificate were a judgment obtained in the Court for a debt of the amount specified in the certificate.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 37(2.3) (src:980)
GIVEN `the certificate is produced to the Federal Court and registered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount specified in the certificate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 37(2.3): the amount of the judgment debt that the certificate has the force and effect of` `the certificate is produced to the Federal Court and registered` `the amount specified in the certificate` MEANS
    IF `the certificate is produced to the Federal Court and registered`
    THEN JUST `the amount specified in the certificate`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (2.4): "may also be registered in the superior court of a province".
-- src:982 | (2.4) A certificate registered under subsection (2.3) may also be registered in the superior court of a province as if it were a document evidencing a judgment of that court.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 37(2.4) (src:982)
GIVEN `the certificate has been registered under subsection 37(2.3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 37(2.4): the certificate may also be registered in the superior court of a province` `the certificate has been registered under subsection 37(2.3)` MEANS
    `the certificate has been registered under subsection 37(2.3)`

-- (2.5): the reasonable costs and charges of registration are recoverable in the same way.
-- src:984 | (2.5) All reasonable costs and charges for the registration of the certificate are recoverable in the same way as if they had been certified and the certificate registered under this section.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 37(2.5) (src:984)
GIVEN `the certificate has been registered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reasonable costs and charges for the registration of the certificate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 37(2.5): the costs and charges that are recoverable in the same way` `the certificate has been registered` `the reasonable costs and charges for the registration of the certificate` MEANS
    IF `the certificate has been registered`
    THEN `the reasonable costs and charges for the registration of the certificate`
    ELSE 0

-- (2.6): a document evidencing a registered certificate may be recorded to create security, a charge, lien or legal hypothec on land in a province held or owned by the debtor.
-- src:986 | (2.6) A document issued by the Federal Court or by a superior court of a province evidencing a certificate in respect of a debtor registered under subsection (2.3) or (2.4) may be recorded for the purpose of creating security, or a charge, lien or legal hypothec, on land in a province, or on an interest in land in a province, held or owned by the debtor, in the same manner as a document evidencing a judgment of the superior court of the province against a person for a debt owing by the person may be recorded in accordance with the law of the province to create security, or a charge, lien or legal hypothec, on land, or an interest in land, held or owned by the person.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 37(2.6) (src:986)
GIVEN `a document issued by the Federal Court or by a superior court of a province evidences a certificate in respect of the debtor registered under subsection 37(2.3) or (2.4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the land, or the interest in land, is in a province and is held or owned by the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 37(2.6): the document may be recorded to create security, or a charge, lien or legal hypothec, on the land` `a document issued by the Federal Court or by a superior court of a province evidences a certificate in respect of the debtor registered under subsection 37(2.3) or (2.4)` `the land, or the interest in land, is in a province and is held or owned by the debtor` MEANS
        `a document issued by the Federal Court or by a superior court of a province evidences a certificate in respect of the debtor registered under subsection 37(2.3) or (2.4)`
    AND `the land, or the interest in land, is in a province and is held or owned by the debtor`

-- (2.7): garnishment of a person who is or is about to become indebted to the debtor, by notice served personally or by confirmed delivery service.
-- src:988 | (2.7) If the Minister knows or suspects that a person is or is about to become indebted or liable to make a payment to a person liable to make a payment to Her Majesty under this Act, the Minister may, by a notice served personally or by confirmed delivery service, require the first person to pay the money otherwise payable to the second person in whole or in part to the Receiver General on account of the second person’s liability.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 37(2.7) (src:988)
GIVEN `the Minister knows or suspects that a person is or is about to become indebted or liable to make a payment to a person liable to make a payment to Her Majesty under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is served personally or by confirmed delivery service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 37(2.7): the Minister may require the first person to pay the money otherwise payable to the second person to the Receiver General` `the Minister knows or suspects that a person is or is about to become indebted or liable to make a payment to a person liable to make a payment to Her Majesty under this Act` `the notice is served personally or by confirmed delivery service` MEANS
        `the Minister knows or suspects that a person is or is about to become indebted or liable to make a payment to a person liable to make a payment to Her Majesty under this Act`
    AND `the notice is served personally or by confirmed delivery service`

-- (2.8): an amount not paid as the notice requires is a debt due to Her Majesty.
-- src:990 | (2.8) An amount not paid as required by a notice under subsection (2.7) is a debt due to Her Majesty.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 37(2.8) (src:990)
GIVEN `the amount not paid as required by a notice under subsection 37(2.7)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 37(2.8): the debt due to Her Majesty for an amount not paid as the notice requires` `the amount not paid as required by a notice under subsection 37(2.7)` MEANS
    `the amount not paid as required by a notice under subsection 37(2.7)`

-- (2.9): an affidavit of personal service is evidence of the service and of the request, notice or demand when it states the three things.
-- src:992 | (2.9) If provision is made by this Act or the regulations for personal service of a request for information or a notice or demand, an affidavit of the person effecting service stating that
-- src:993 | (a) the person has charge of the appropriate records and has knowledge of the facts in the particular case,
-- src:994 | (b) such a request, notice or demand was served personally on a named day on the person to whom it was directed, and
-- src:995 | (c) the person identifies as an exhibit attached to the affidavit a true copy of the request, notice or demand,
-- src:996 | is evidence of the personal service and of the request, notice or demand.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 37(2.9) (src:992-996)
GIVEN `provision is made by this Act or the regulations for personal service of a request for information or a notice or demand` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit states that the person has charge of the appropriate records and has knowledge of the facts in the particular case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit states that such a request, notice or demand was served personally on a named day on the person to whom it was directed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person identifies as an exhibit attached to the affidavit a true copy of the request, notice or demand` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 37(2.9): the affidavit is evidence of the personal service and of the request, notice or demand` `provision is made by this Act or the regulations for personal service of a request for information or a notice or demand` `the affidavit states that the person has charge of the appropriate records and has knowledge of the facts in the particular case` `the affidavit states that such a request, notice or demand was served personally on a named day on the person to whom it was directed` `the person identifies as an exhibit attached to the affidavit a true copy of the request, notice or demand` MEANS
        `provision is made by this Act or the regulations for personal service of a request for information or a notice or demand`
    AND `the affidavit states that the person has charge of the appropriate records and has knowledge of the facts in the particular case`
    AND `the affidavit states that such a request, notice or demand was served personally on a named day on the person to whom it was directed`
    AND `the person identifies as an exhibit attached to the affidavit a true copy of the request, notice or demand`

-- The whole debt of a person: the three debts of subsections (2), (2.01) and (2.02) added together. The debt of (2.8) is owed by the person who was served
-- with the notice and did not pay, not by the person whose debtor they are, so it is not added. No provision states a total, so this is a helper
-- (the `oa1: ` prefix) and carries no `@ref`; the debts it adds are the rules above.
GIVEN `the debt for a benefit payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the debt for interest` IS A NUMBER
      `the debt for a penalty` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`oa1: the total of a person's debts for a payment, interest and a penalty` `the debt for a benefit payment` `the debt for interest` `the debt for a penalty` MEANS
    `the debt for a benefit payment` PLUS `the debt for interest` PLUS `the debt for a penalty`

-- (4): the Minister may remit all or any portion of the amount if satisfied of any of (a) to (d), unless the person has been convicted of an offence
-- under any provision of this Act or of the Criminal Code in connection with obtaining the payment.
-- src:999 | (4) Notwithstanding subsections (1), (2) and (3), where a person has received or obtained a benefit payment to which that person is not entitled or a benefit payment in excess of the amount of the benefit payment to which that person is entitled and the Minister is satisfied that
-- src:1000 | (a) the amount or excess of the benefit payment cannot be collected within the reasonably foreseeable future,
-- src:1001 | (b) the administrative costs of collecting the amount or excess of the benefit payment are likely to equal or exceed the amount to be collected,
-- src:1002 | (c) repayment of the amount or excess of the benefit payment would cause undue hardship to the debtor, or
-- src:1003 | (d) the amount or excess of the benefit payment is the result of erroneous advice or administrative error in the administration of this Act,
-- src:1004 | the Minister may, unless that person has been convicted of an offence under any provision of this Act or of the Criminal Code in connection with the obtaining of the benefit payment, remit all or any portion of the amount or excess of the benefit payment.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 37(4) (src:999-1004)
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that the amount or excess of the benefit payment cannot be collected within the reasonably foreseeable future` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that the administrative costs of collecting the amount or excess of the benefit payment are likely to equal or exceed the amount to be collected` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that repayment of the amount or excess of the benefit payment would cause undue hardship to the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that the amount or excess of the benefit payment is the result of erroneous advice or administrative error in the administration of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been convicted of an offence under any provision of this Act or of the Criminal Code in connection with the obtaining of the benefit payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 37(4): the Minister may remit all or any portion of the amount or excess of the benefit payment` `the Minister is satisfied that the amount or excess of the benefit payment cannot be collected within the reasonably foreseeable future` `the Minister is satisfied that the administrative costs of collecting the amount or excess of the benefit payment are likely to equal or exceed the amount to be collected` `the Minister is satisfied that repayment of the amount or excess of the benefit payment would cause undue hardship to the debtor` `the Minister is satisfied that the amount or excess of the benefit payment is the result of erroneous advice or administrative error in the administration of this Act` `the person has been convicted of an offence under any provision of this Act or of the Criminal Code in connection with the obtaining of the benefit payment` MEANS
        (    `the Minister is satisfied that the amount or excess of the benefit payment cannot be collected within the reasonably foreseeable future`
         OR  `the Minister is satisfied that the administrative costs of collecting the amount or excess of the benefit payment are likely to equal or exceed the amount to be collected`
         OR  `the Minister is satisfied that repayment of the amount or excess of the benefit payment would cause undue hardship to the debtor`
         OR  `the Minister is satisfied that the amount or excess of the benefit payment is the result of erroneous advice or administrative error in the administration of this Act`)
    AND (NOT `the person has been convicted of an offence under any provision of this Act or of the Criminal Code in connection with the obtaining of the benefit payment`)

-- (5): "Section 155.1 of the Financial Administration Act does not apply in relation to amounts owing to Her Majesty under this Act".
-- src:1006 | (5) Section 155.1 of the Financial Administration Act does not apply in relation to amounts owing to Her Majesty under this Act.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 37(5) (src:1006)
GIVEN `the amount is owing to Her Majesty under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 37(5): section 155.1 of the Financial Administration Act applies in relation to the amount` `the amount is owing to Her Majesty under this Act` MEANS
    FALSE
